    "The dated 2026–2027 handbook controls over the older chart and chair-group list. The common compulsory cluster says to take all its courses and totals 111 credits. Individual API required flags do not override that cluster rule. General, laboratory and fieldwork safety carry zero credits and precede the relevant practical activities.",
    "Year one has 51 compulsory credits, a three-credit conditional foundation and six biology credits. Year two has 60 compulsory credits. Corrected the earlier weights for transport, building physics, time-dependent mathematics, business economics, process basics and sustainability transitions; added the missing dynamic-modelling module and current introduction, statistics, linear-algebra and agricultural-systems-analysis components.",
    "The example selects the Mathematics B entry branch and Statistics 1. Mathematics A entrants take Mathematics Applied: Introduction instead. The first listed biology option is Principles of Animal Nutrition; the first nonduplicated third-year option is Grassland Science. Adviser consultation remains an explicit condition. Selection follows catalogue order without reference to UCR fit. The published exclusion concerning two plant-biology courses does not affect this pair.",
    "111 compulsory credits, three foundation credits, twelve restricted biology credits and the 24-credit thesis total 150. Optional robotics packages of zero, six or twelve credits and other technical options of zero to eighteen credits can occupy the remaining thirty credits. They are not additional compulsory requirements. This example leaves thirty credits genuinely open for a minor, individual minor or electives. No mandatory placement is listed.",
    "The programme and thesis entry agree on 102 credits from compulsory and restricted courses, all first-year courses, Data Analysis for Biosystems Engineering and Research Methods Biosystems Engineering. Completing the first two years supplies 120 credits and satisfies these conditions before the thesis. The third year contains biology six, thesis twenty-four and open study thirty credits.",
    "The thesis is individually supervised inquiry: analyse a problem, prepare a plan, examine literature, execute the plan, write a report and present orally. Experiments are conducted where needed. The supervisor can agree a start at any time of year. Neither original discovery nor laboratory experiments are universally required.",
    "The current profile, outcomes and actual course entries establish integrated living-production technology with mathematical analysis, physical systems, sensing, control, design, biology, economics and society. The current handbook supplies adequate formal detail; no material unresolved conflict requires an additional regulation search."
